{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1866","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"H. Happy Sets"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Define a set $$$A$$$ as a child of set $$$B$$$ if and only if for each element of value $$$x$$$ that is in $$$A$$$, there exists an element of value $$$x+1$$$ that is in $$$B$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given integers $$$N$$$ and $$$K$$$. In order to make Chaneka happy, you must find the number of different arrays containing $$$N$$$ sets $$$[S_1, S_2, S_3, \\ldots, S_N]$$$ such that: - Each set can only contain zero or more different integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$K$$$. - There exists a way to rearrange the order of the array of sets into $$$[S'_1, S'_2, S'_3, \\ldots, S'_N]$$$ such that $$$S'_i$$$ is a child of $$$S'_{i+1}$$$ for each $$$1\\leq i\\leq N-1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the answer modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Two sets are considered different if and only if there is at least one value that only occurs in one of the two sets."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Two arrays of sets are considered different if and only if there is at least one index $$$i$$$ such that the sets at index $$$i$$$ in the two arrays are different."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"at